u_n^2}{8} ight) - \exp(-\{ w(\mc{T}) \vee \log n\})$, where $\psi(\varepsilon, d/n)$ is defined in \eqref{eq:lowerbound} below.  egin{equation*} 
norm{\wh{\Pi}^{\T} \mathbf{y} - \Pi^{*\T} \mathbf{y}}_2 \leq  rac{2 (1 + \sqrt{2})\sigma \varepsilon^{-2} \{w(\mc{T}) \vee \log n\}}{\sqrt{n}}. \end{equation*} \end{lemma}  egin{proof} In view of Lemma ef{lem:decoupling}, by definition of $\wh{\Pi}^{\T}$ and the fact that $\Pi^{*\T}$ is a feasible solution, we have  egin{align*} &
